# JAYSTARBLISS STUDIOS — MASTER PORTAL REDESIGN, UX ARCHITECTURE, RESPONSIVENESS AND FEATURE-PARITY IMPLEMENTATION

## 1. MISSION

You are the principal product designer, senior frontend architect, full-stack engineer, accessibility specialist, responsive-design engineer and QA lead responsible for redesigning the **entire existing Jaystarbliss Studios / Jaystarbliss Dynamic Institute authenticated platform**.

The objective is to transform the current dashboards into a coherent, professional, modern, easy-to-use education SaaS experience across desktop, tablet and mobile.

This is not a superficial restyling exercise. The current system contains unnecessary text, repetitive cards, inconsistent headers, dense interfaces, oversized content sections, inconsistent component styling and layouts that do not always use available screen space effectively. Some features also appear differently across roles or are repeated unnecessarily.

We need a better architecture for the user experience while preserving the underlying application.

**NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE: REDESIGN THE EXPERIENCE, NOT THE BUSINESS LOGIC. Preserve every existing capability, route, data relationship, permission boundary, integration, and working workflow unless an explicitly authorised defect correction requires a change. Nothing may disappear merely because it is difficult to fit into the new design.**

Do not create a new application. Do not replace the existing authentication system. Do not delete features to make the interface appear simpler. Do not rebuild the whole platform from memory or rely solely on screenshots.

Inspect the real code, establish a feature inventory, redesign systematically, implement the changes, test them, correct regressions and document the actual result.

Use Claude Opus 5.5 if that model is genuinely available in the active environment. Otherwise, use the strongest suitable available model and proceed.

