## 18. SAFETY AND CHANGE MANAGEMENT

Before modifying files, inspect the Git state and preserve existing local changes.

Work on a feature branch if possible. Never force-push, reset, discard uncommitted work or overwrite unrelated changes.

Do not execute destructive production migrations or alter live security rules as part of a UI redesign without appropriate authorisation, an understood rollback plan and explicit evidence that the change is necessary.

Do not fabricate data, delete real records, alter role definitions, remove API endpoints or modify the Firestore schema merely to simplify the presentation.

Do not mark a control complete just because it looks right. It must perform its intended action and give the user accurate feedback.

Do not claim that production has been updated because the local build passes. Report the actual commit, deployment status and live verification evidence where those can be established.

